sequenceDiagram
    participant Author as Engineer (authoring)
    participant Status as 00-status.md
    participant ProgDoc as 03-program-design.md
    participant EpicDoc as epic-<id>-design.md
    participant BuildIndex as build_index.py
    participant IndexJson as data/index.json
    participant Viewer as viewer/index.html
    participant Sheet as design-doc sheet (openAdrSheet pattern)
    participant Reader as Engineer (reading)

    Author->>Status: Marks Gate 3 / Gate 4b approved
    Author->>ProgDoc: Writes program-design doc
    Author->>EpicDoc: Writes epic technical-design doc

    Note over BuildIndex: Index rebuild (odyssey / implement modes call this)
    BuildIndex->>Status: resolve_feature_gates() parses gate approval state
    BuildIndex->>ProgDoc: project_fields(source, fields) reads doc if present
    BuildIndex->>EpicDoc: project_fields(source, fields) reads doc if present
    BuildIndex->>IndexJson: Writes program_design entity keyed by feature_slug
    BuildIndex->>IndexJson: Writes epic_design entity keyed by epic id
    BuildIndex->>IndexJson: Writes joins.feature_gates with doc-reference field per gate

    Reader->>Viewer: Opens Builds view
    Viewer->>IndexJson: Reads window.INDEX
    Viewer->>Viewer: renderBuildsMainContent() renders gate-rail-grid
    Viewer->>Viewer: renderEpicCard() adds design-doc chip when epic_design is approved

    Reader->>Viewer: Clicks a gate card in gate-rail-grid
    Viewer->>Sheet: openGateDesignSheet(feature_slug, gate_n)
    Sheet->>IndexJson: Looks up joins.feature_gates doc reference
    Sheet-->>Reader: Renders program-design doc content, read-only

    Reader->>Viewer: Clicks a design-doc chip on an epic card
    Viewer->>Sheet: openGateDesignSheet(epic_id, scope="epic")
    Sheet->>IndexJson: Looks up epic_design entity by epic id
    Sheet-->>Reader: Renders epic technical-design doc content, read-only
